course: dictionary
lesson: 5350
title: The kilogram
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kilogram is a unit for measuring how heavy something is. Scientists call this mass. A bag of sugar often weighs one kilogram, so you can picture it in your hands.
explain: The short form is kg, so 2 kilograms is written 2 kg. Kilo is the informal word people use in shops, like «two kilos of apples».
explain: One kilogram is 1000 grams. So half a kilogram is 500 grams, and 2 kilograms is 2000 grams. To change kilograms into grams, multiply by 1000.
fact: A kilogram is the basic unit of mass, and scales are used to measure it.
fact: 1 kilogram = 1000 grams.
fact: Shops often sell fruit, flour and meat by the kilogram, and the price is given per kilogram.
fact: «A newborn elephant calf weighs about 100 kilograms at birth.»
fact: «Giant tortoises can weigh over 200 kilograms.»
exercise: What is a kilogram used to measure? | How far away a place is | How long something is | *How heavy something is
exercise: «A sheep called Shrek grew 27 kilograms of wool.» How many grams is that? | 2700 grams | *27000 grams | 270 grams
exercise: Apples cost 3 pounds per kilogram, and Sam buys 2 kilograms. How much does he pay? | 32 pounds | 3 pounds | 5 pounds | *6 pounds
test: How many grams are in half a kilogram? | 50 grams | *500 grams | 5000 grams | 250 grams
test: Which is the short form of kilogram? | *kg | kl | g | kgm
exam: «A giant tortoise can weigh over 200 kilograms.» Roughly how many grams is that? | 200 grams | 20000 grams | *200000 grams | 2000 grams
